{
  "_readme": [
    "Golden query set for scripts/evaluate-retrieval.mjs.",
    "Each entry: { query, expected, notes? }.",
    "  query    — a natural-language search a real user would type.",
    "  expected — cafe names that SHOULD appear in the top results.",
    "             Case-insensitive substring match against the cafe `name`",
    "             column, so 'Anchorhead' matches 'Anchorhead Coffee'.",
    "  notes    — optional, why these cafes are the right answer.",
    "Entries with an empty `expected` run in TRIAGE mode: the script prints",
    "their top-5 results so you can inspect them and fill in `expected`.",
    "Labels drafted from DB tags + LLM evidence quotes, then human-reviewed.",
    "Grow this list from real searches in the nl_query_log table (aim for 30-50).",
    "An expected entry may be written \"Name @ Neighborhood\" when the bare name",
    "cannot identify one cafe (\"Starbucks Coffee Company\" matches 29 rows across",
    "15 neighborhoods). Unqualified chain names score a hit on whichever branch",
    "happens to rank, anywhere, which makes the metric meaningless for that query."
